commit 9ba565481083a91c3e098786fd1a834f7d7f5b2a
Author: a11 <augstar@gmail.com>
Date:   Thu Jul 16 16:34:43 2026 +0300

    feat(onboarding): durable operator hardware-trust approval path (#582)
    
    Closes the primary provider-onboarding deadlock: a hardware-verification job
    parked in status=waiting_trust had no operator API — the only way to promote it
    was hand-editing stats-hardware-inventory.yaml and waiting on two systemd timers,
    and stats-inventory-sync would DELETE any out-of-band trust row on its next run.
    
    Adds a dual-control operator approval path that survives sync, mirroring the
    provider_auth_policy SECURITY DEFINER pattern so the coordinator's
    provider_onboarding role never gains raw write on hardware_verification_trust
    (the deliberate anti-fraud boundary is preserved):
    
    - migration 018: source column on hardware_verification_trust (inventory|operator_api);
      hardware_trust_pending/_grants tables; request/approve SECURITY DEFINER fns owned
      by new NOLOGIN hardware_trust_definer role; EXECUTE split requester/approver.
    - stats-inventory-sync: tag upserts source='inventory', scope its DELETE to
      source='inventory' so operator_api approvals persist.
    - coordinator: separate request/approve DB handles + two new DSNs; dual-control
      endpoints POST /admin/hardware-trust/approve + /approve/{id}/approve; read
      endpoint GET /admin/hardware-trust/waiting (lists waiting_trust jobs).
    
    Approved trust roots feed the existing stats-hardware-verifier, which promotes
    the job through its normal validation — no bypass. Rollout gated on Pearl
    provisioning the 3 NOLOGIN roles + two DSNs.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>

